 DIGITAL FORENSICS INVESTIGATION & TRIAGEFINAL INVESTIGATION REPORTCase ID: CIP-B104-CS3-C11_26_DFIT_17300Case Name: RHINOUSBInvestigator: Simon Friday AdekaDate of Investigation: 03 - 04 September 2026Location: Abuja, NigeriaCourse: CIP-B104 Computer Forensics1. EXECUTIVE SUMMARYThis report documents the forensic acquisition, analysis, and recovery of data from a USB storage device labeled RHINOUSB. The objective was to apply the DFIT methodology to identify deleted files and hidden data. 
Two key files were recovered. File 1 contained a passphrase which was used to extract steganographic data from File 2. The extracted evidence is documented and all integrity hashes are maintained for chain of custody.2. EVIDENCE DESCRIPTIONItem #DescriptionSerial/LabelHash AlgorithmHash ValueE001Original ImageRHINOUSB.ddSHA256See Screenshot 0E002Working CopyRHINOUSB_working.ddSHA256Verified MatchE003Recovered Docf0335017_She_died_in_February_at_the_age_of_74.docMD5/SHA256See Section 5E004Recovered Imagef0335081.jpgMD5/SHA256See Section 5E005Extracted Textextracted_evidence.txtSHA2562545063f0580a80936bd999b60b683d66e565c0004f84b28e9740afaaa87ae5b3. TOOLS AND METHODOLOGYThe investigation followed DFIT 5-Step Process:Acquisition: dd was used to create a forensic image. SHA256 was used to verify integrity.Preservation: Working copy was used. Original was write-protected.Analysis: Sleuth Kit tools mmls, fsstat, fls were used. FAT16 file system detected.Recovery: PhotoRec was used for data carving of deleted files.Documentation: All steps were screenshot and hashed. Steghide was used for steganography detection.Tools Used: Kali Linux 2026.2, dd, Sleuth Kit 4.12, PhotoRec 7.2, steghide 0.5.14. FINDINGSFile System: The USB device was formatted as FAT16 with 1 primary partition.File Recovery: PhotoRec successfully recovered f0335017_She_died_in_February_at_the_age_of_74.doc and f0335081.jpg from unallocated space.Steganography: Analysis of f0335081.jpg revealed steganographic data. The passphrase She died in February at the age of 74 was found in the filename of File 1.Extracted Evidence: Using steghide extract -sf f0335081.jpg -p "She died in February at the age of 74", the file extracted_evidence.txt was recovered. The content references events in August 2001 and personal relationships.5. EVIDENCE HASH SUMMARYTo maintain chain of custody, the following hashes were generated:File NameMD5SHA256f0335017_She_died_in_February_at_the_age_of_74.docf0335081.jpgextracted_evidence.txt2545063f0580a80936bd999b60b683d66e565c0004f84b28e9740afaaa87ae5b6. CONCLUSIONThe forensic investigation of RHINOUSB was completed successfully following DFIT standards. Deleted files were recovered and steganographic data was extracted and documented. The integrity of all evidence was maintained through hashing and documentation. The extracted data from extracted_evidence.txt may be relevant to the ongoing investigation.All supporting screenshots and evidence files are included in the GitHub repository.7. APPENDIXA. Screenshot ManifestB. Master Provenance CSVC. Command LogInvestigator Signature: _**____Date: 04 September 2026TO CREATE THE PDFCopy this into LibreOffice / Google DocsFile > Download > PDFName it: Final_Report.pdfMove to folder: 05_Reports/Final_Report.pdfUpdate README.md: *Full Report:* 05_Reports/Final_Report.pdf``Run the md5sum and sha256sum commands I gave you before and fill in the [INSERT] parts in Section 5.Need me to format this as an actual .docx or do you want me to add your real name + ID on the signature line?
